    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThanks a lot for such a great plugin!\r\n\r\n`mini.files` fails to update the displayed filename when a file is renamed, specifically when changing the case of the filename (e.g., from `someFile.lua` to `somefile.lua`). Although the `mini.files` correctly recognizes the changed filename after synchronizing changes, the displayed filename does not update accordingly after accepting the changes.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-562+gf0884f21f-Homebrew\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Open Neovim\r\n2. Execute the command `:lua MiniFiles.open()`\r\n3. Enter insert mode and add a file named `someFile.lua`\r\n4. Execute the command `:lua MiniFiles.synchronize()` and accept changes \r\n5. Locate the file `someFile.lua` and rename it to `somefile.lua` (changing the case to lowercase)\r\n6. Execute the command `:lua MiniFiles.synchronize()` and accept changes \r\n7. Observe that the file name has not changed, despite `mini.files` correctly recognizing the updated filename\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`someFile.lua` changes to `somefile.lua` after renaming, synchronizing and accepting changes.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nFilename doesn't change, despite `mini.files` recognizing the updated filename.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/33033411/a935c22e-c8f6-4f47-8430-432af1b05ec9\r\n\r\n",
